teach_text = "Think about what happens if someone says there is a shapeshifter in their own class. What role(s) could they have?"
bottom_out_text = "If we inspect A1, we can see they have to be a shapeshifter to avoid creating a contradiction. Next, A2 and B3 have to be innocent, because someone claiming their own innocence has to be innocent, no matter if they lie or tell the truth. This means A3 lies, so they are innocent. If A3 lies, there must be a shapeshifting wizard, so all witches are innocent, and therefore tell the truth. By C1, we know that B1 is innocent, meaning the second shapeshifter is the last wizard, C3."

